# IDUs — IDU-scientist

Version {{VERSION}}. Self-contained academic writing skills:

- [idus-draft](skills/idus-draft/SKILL.md): first versions from research notes and author intent.
- [idus-review](skills/idus-review/SKILL.md): audit and authorised edits of existing prose.
- [idus-configure](skills/idus-configure/SKILL.md): project rules/terms and expert-derived proposals.

Copy complete skill folders to a supported skill directory, or use:

```text
npx skills add DDonnyy/IDUs --copy
```

Claude can load this plugin with `claude --plugin-dir path/to/IDUs`. The repository also supplies
portable/Codex manifests and a Claude marketplace. Runtime draft needs no Python; optional helpers
in review/configure use Python 3.10+ standard library. Install only the skills needed.

Original toolkit: Apache-2.0, [LICENSE](LICENSE), [NOTICE](NOTICE),
[source rights](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). Private archives/project settings are excluded.
